      <div class="callout"><p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> the best cold email campaign platform for most teams in 2026 is a dedicated outreach tool: Instantly, Smartlead, lemlist or ManyReach. HubSpot, Zoho Campaigns, Mailchimp, Brevo and MailerLite are excellent email marketing tools, but they are built for opted-in subscribers, not cold prospects.</p></div>
      <p>That distinction decides everything. Below is an honest comparison of the best email marketing tools and cold email software of 2026: what each costs, what each is really for, and where each one can get your account suspended. Prices were checked in late September 2026 and change often, so confirm on each vendor's pricing page before you buy.</p>

      <h2 id="sec1">Cold email platforms vs email marketing platforms: what's the difference?</h2>
      <p>An email campaign is a coordinated series of emails with one goal. Where your list came from decides which tool you can use.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Email marketing platforms</strong> (HubSpot, Zoho Campaigns, Mailchimp, Brevo, MailerLite) send newsletters and promotions to people who signed up. They run on shared sending infrastructure and expect provable consent.</li>
        <li><strong>Cold email platforms</strong> (Instantly, Smartlead, lemlist, ManyReach) send one-to-one outreach to prospects who haven't opted in. They connect many mailboxes, warm them up, and throttle volume so no single domain burns.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Mailchimp's acceptable use policy bans purchased, rented, third-party and partner lists, and it can suspend accounts that break the rule. Most traditional senders enforce the same standard. Upload a prospect list to one of them and you risk the account and your domain's reputation. It is the most expensive mistake in this category.</p>

      <h2 id="sec2">Top email marketing platforms and email campaign tools compared (2026)</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap">
